3. Spring Boot
Definition

Spring Boot is a framework built on top of Spring Framework used to create production-ready Java applications quickly.

It reduces configuration and provides:

Embedded server
Dependency injection
REST API support
Database integration
Advantages
1. Auto Configuration

Spring Boot automatically configures required components.

Example:

Instead of manually configuring:

DispatcherServlet
Database Connection
Tomcat Server

Spring Boot handles it.

