5. Creating REST API in Spring Boot
REST API
Definition

REST (Representational State Transfer) is an architecture used for communication between frontend and backend using HTTP methods.

Common methods:

Method	Purpose
GET	Fetch data
POST	Create data
PUT	Update data
DELETE	Remove data

Example:

Library System:

GET /books

POST /books

PUT /books/1

DELETE /books/1
6. Spring Boot Controller

Controller handles incoming requests.

Example:

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/books")
public class BookController {


@GetMapping
public String getBooks(){

return "All Books";

}


@PostMapping
public String addBook(){

return "Book Added";

}

}

Request:

localhost:8080/books

Response:

All Books
